# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum computers {#quantum-computers}"
msgstr "量子コンピューター {#quantum-computers}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bits $\\rightarrow$ qubits {#bits-rightarrow-qubits}"
msgstr "ビット $\\rightarrow$ qubit {#bits-rightarrow-qubits}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Just as bits are the fundamental units of classical information, *quantum* bits, or \"qubits,\" are the fundamental units of quantum information. Like the classical bit, the state of a qubit can be either 0 or 1, which we typically denote as $\\vert 0\\rangle$ and $\\vert 1\\rangle$. But unlike the classical bit, a quantum bit can also be in a *superposition* of both the $\\vert 0\\rangle$ state and the $\\vert 1\\rangle$ state at the same time. In general, a qubit can be in any state $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ of the form:\n"
msgstr "ビットが古典的な情報の基本単位であるように、*量子*ビット（qubit）は量子情報の基本単位です。古典的なビットと同様に、Qubitの状態は0または1のいずれかで、通常$\\vert 0\\rangle$および$\\vert 1\\rangle$と表記します。しかし古典的なビットとは異なり、量子ビットは$\\vert 0\\rangle$状態と$\\vert 1\\rangle$状態の両方の*重ね合わせ*に同時になることができます。一般に、Qubitは以下の形式の任意の状態$\\vert \\psi\\rangle$になれます：\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi\\rangle = c_0 \\vert 0\\rangle + c_1 \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi\\rangle = c_0 \\vert 0\\rangle + c_1 \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $c_0$ and $c_1$ are complex amplitudes with $\\vert c_0 \\vert ^2+\\vert c_1\\vert ^2=1$.\n"
msgstr "ここで$c_0$および$c_1$は$\\vert c_0 \\vert ^2+\\vert c_1\\vert ^2=1$を満たす複素振幅です。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "The quantum phase {#the-quantum-phase}"
msgstr "量子位相 {#the-quantum-phase}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Because $c_0$ and $c_1$ are complex, they can each be written as $c_i = \\vert c_i\\vert e^{i\\phi_i}$ where $\\phi_i$ is called the *phase*. If we multiply the whole state by the same overall phase factor, nothing physically changes — this is called a global phase, and it has no observable consequences.\n"
msgid "Because $c_0$ and $c_1$ are complex, they can each be written as $c_j = \\vert c_j\\vert e^{i\\phi_j}$ where $\\phi_j$ is called the *phase*. If we multiply the whole state by the same overall phase factor, nothing physically changes — this is called a global phase, and it has no observable consequences.\n"
msgstr "$c_0$と$c_1$は複素数であるため、それぞれ$c_i = \\vert c_i\\vert e^{i\\phi_i}$と書けます。ここで$\\phi_i$は*位相*と呼ばれます。状態全体に同じ全体位相因子を乗算しても、物理的には何も変わりません——これをグローバル位相と呼び、観測可能な影響はありません。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For that reason, it is conventional to “factor out” $e^{i\\phi_0}$, giving:\n"
msgstr "そのため、$e^{i\\phi_0}$を「括り出す」ことが慣例となっており、次のように書けます：\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$\\vert \\psi\\rangle = \\vert c_0\\vert \\vert 0\\rangle + \\vert c_1\\vert e^{i\\phi}\\vert 1\\rangle$$\n"
msgstr "$$\\vert \\psi\\rangle = \\vert c_0\\vert \\vert 0\\rangle + \\vert c_1\\vert e^{i\\phi}\\vert 1\\rangle$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $\\phi = \\phi_1-\\phi_0$ is the *relative* phase of the quantum state, which *does* have observable consequences.\n"
msgstr "ここで$\\phi = \\phi_1-\\phi_0$は量子状態の*相対*位相であり、これは観測可能な影響を*持ちます*。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This phase plays a very important role in quantum computing, and you will explore its various consequences in the subsequent Qiskit in the Classroom modules.\n"
msgstr "この位相は量子コンピューティングにおいて非常に重要な役割を果たしており、続くQiskit in the Classroomモジュールでその様々な影響を探求していきます。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Multiple qubits {#multiple-qubits}"
msgstr "複数のQubit {#multiple-qubits}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "While the state of multiple bits could simply be expressed as a string of 0s and 1s, the state of multiple qubits gets a little more complicated because of the principles of *superposition* and *entanglement*.\n"
msgstr "複数のビットの状態は単純に0と1の文字列で表せますが、複数のQubitの状態は*重ね合わせ*と*エンタングルメント*の原理により、少し複雑になります。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Recall that $N$ bits could be in one of $2^N$ possible states ranging from binary numbers 000...000 to 111...111. But now, because of the principle of superposition, $N$ *qubits* can be in a superposition of *all* of these states at once!\n"
msgstr "$N$ビットは二進数の000...000から111...111までの$2^N$通りの可能な状態のうちの1つになれることを思い出してください。しかし今度は重ね合わせの原理により、$N$個の*qubit*はこれらすべての状態の重ね合わせに*同時に*なることができます！\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This can be expressed as\n"
msgstr "これは次のように表現できます：\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\psi_N = \\sum_{j=0}^{2^N-1} c_j \\vert j\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\psi_N = \\sum_{j=0}^{2^N-1} c_j \\vert j\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "where, as in the classical case, the state $\\vert i\\rangle$ corresponds to the state where each qubit is in the right combination of 0s and 1s to yield the binary number $i$. These are known as the \"computational basis states\" of the quantum system. For example, a three-qubit state can be written as a superposition of its eight computational basis states:\n"
msgid "where, as in the classical case, the state $\\vert j\\rangle$ corresponds to the state where each qubit is in the right combination of 0s and 1s to yield the binary number $j$. These are known as the \"computational basis states\" of the quantum system. For example, a three-qubit state can be written as a superposition of its eight computational basis states:\n"
msgstr "ここで古典的な場合と同様に、状態$\\vert i\\rangle$は各Qubitが0と1の適切な組み合わせになって二進数$i$を生成する状態に対応します。これらは量子系の「計算基底状態」として知られています。例えば、3Qubit状態はその8つの計算基底状態の重ね合わせとして書けます：\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\psi_3 = c_0 \\vert 000\\rangle + c_1 \\vert 001\\rangle + c_2 \\vert 010\\rangle + c_3 \\vert 011\\rangle + c_4 \\vert 100\\rangle + c_5 \\vert 101\\rangle + c_6 \\vert 110\\rangle + c_7 \\vert 111\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\psi_3 = c_0 \\vert 000\\rangle + c_1 \\vert 001\\rangle + c_2 \\vert 010\\rangle + c_3 \\vert 011\\rangle + c_4 \\vert 100\\rangle + c_5 \\vert 101\\rangle + c_6 \\vert 110\\rangle + c_7 \\vert 111\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each qubit in the system is denoted with an index $0$ through $N-1$. The convention is to read the qubit states from right to left, so that the state of qubit $0$ is the rightmost state and the state of qubit $N-1$ is the leftmost. This is known as \"little-endian\" notation, and it may seem counterintuitive at first, since we're used to reading left to right.\n"
msgstr "系の各Qubitはインデックス$0$から$N-1$で示されます。慣例として、Qubitの状態は右から左に読みます。つまりQubit $0$の状態が最右端で、qubit $N-1$の状態が最左端になります。これは「リトルエンディアン」記法として知られており、左から右に読むことに慣れているため、最初は直感に反して感じるかもしれません。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-2}"
msgstr "理解度チェック {#check-your-understanding-2}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At first glance, it may seem counterintuitive to order the qubits from right to left as in little-endian notation, but it's actually a very logical thing to do! Explain why. (Recall our discussion above of binary to base-10 number conversion.)\n"
msgstr "一見すると、リトルエンディアン記法のようにQubitを右から左に並べることは直感に反するように思えるかもしれませんが、実は非常に論理的なことです！その理由を説明してください。（上記の二進数から10進数への変換の話を思い出してください。）\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If we order qubits from right to left, so that qubit 0 is the farthest right and qubit N-1 is the farthest left, It is logical to associate qubit $0$ with the least-significant bit, which is multiplied by $2^0$ and qubit $N-1$ with the most-significant bit, which is multiplied by $2^{N-1}$.\n"
msgstr "Qubitを右から左に並べ、qubit 0が最右端でQubit N-1が最左端になるようにすると、qubit $0$を$2^0$で乗算される最下位ビットに対応させ、qubit $N-1$を$2^{N-1}$で乗算される最上位ビットに対応させることが論理的です。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Entanglement {#entanglement}"
msgstr "エンタングルメント {#entanglement}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As we mentioned earlier, another key feature of qubits is that they can be *entangled* with one another. Let's take an example of a two-qubit state, where $c_0 = c_3 = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$ and $c_1 = c_2 = 0$:\n"
msgstr "先ほど述べたように、Qubitのもう1つの重要な特徴は、互いに*エンタングル*できることです。$c_0 = c_3 = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$、$c_1 = c_2 = 0$の2Qubit状態の例を見てみましょう：\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$\\vert \\psi\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(\\vert 00\\rangle + \\vert 11\\rangle)$$\n"
msgstr "$$\\vert \\psi\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(\\vert 00\\rangle + \\vert 11\\rangle)$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "So, the state of qubit 0 can be either $\\vert 0\\rangle$ or $\\vert 1\\rangle$ with equal probability, and same with the state of qubit 1. But these probabilities are no longer independent of one another. If we find the state of qubit 0 to be $\\vert 0\\rangle$, then we *know* that qubit 1 will also be in $\\vert 0\\rangle$. This is true no matter how far apart one another, which is why the act of measuring an entangled state is sometimes referred to as \"spooky action at a distance.\"\n"
msgstr "つまり、qubit 0の状態は等しい確率で$\\vert 0\\rangle$または$\\vert 1\\rangle$になり得て、qubit 1も同様です。しかし、これらの確率はもはや互いに独立ではありません。qubit 0の状態が$\\vert 0\\rangle$とわかれば、qubit 1も$\\vert 0\\rangle$にあることが*わかります*。これは互いにどれだけ離れていても成り立つため、エンタングルした状態を測定する行為はときに「不気味な遠隔作用」と呼ばれます。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Entanglement can also take other forms. For example, the state\n"
msgstr "エンタングルメントは他の形でも現れます。例えば、状態\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$\\vert \\psi\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(\\vert 01\\rangle + \\vert 10\\rangle)$$\n"
msgstr "$$\\vert \\psi\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(\\vert 01\\rangle + \\vert 10\\rangle)$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "produces opposite outcomes every time: if one qubit is measured $\\vert 0\\rangle$, the other is guaranteed to be found in the $\\vert 1\\rangle$ state.\n"
msgstr "は常に反対の結果をもたらします：一方のQubitが$\\vert 0\\rangle$と測定されれば、もう一方は必ず$\\vert 1\\rangle$の状態で見つかります。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-3}"
msgstr "理解度チェック {#check-your-understanding-3}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Is the state $\\vert \\psi\\rangle = \\vert 11\\rangle$ entangled? Why or why not?\n"
msgstr "状態$\\vert \\psi\\rangle = \\vert 11\\rangle$はエンタングルしていますか？その理由を答えてください。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It is not entangled. While the outcomes are always the same when you measure both qubits, this is only because each qubit is always fixed in the state $\\vert 1\\rangle$. The result of measuring one qubit does not actually depend on the other — both are just always $\\vert 1\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "エンタングルしていません。両方のQubitを測定すると結果が常に同じになりますが、これは各Qubitが常に$\\vert 1\\rangle$の状態に固定されているためです。一方のQubitを測定した結果は実際にはもう一方に依存しておらず、どちらも常に$\\vert 1\\rangle$なのです。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In general, if you can describe each qubit’s state separately and then multiply them together like this:\n"
msgstr "一般に、各Qubitの状態を個別に記述してから次のように積を取ることができる場合：\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$\\vert \\psi\\rangle = \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle \\vert \\psi_0\\rangle $$\n"
msgstr "$$\\vert \\psi\\rangle = \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle \\vert \\psi_0\\rangle $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Then it is known as a \"product state\" and is *not* entangled.\n"
msgstr "これは「積状態」として知られており、エンタングル*していません*。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Vector notation {#vector-notation}"
msgstr "ベクトル記法 {#vector-notation}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It is often helpful to use vectors and matrices to see how the quantum state transforms under different operations. In this representation, our quantum states will be vectors, and our quantum gates (discussed in the next section) will be matrices that transform the vectors.\n"
msgstr "量子状態が異なる演算の下でどのように変換されるかを確認するには、ベクトルと行列を使用すると便利です。この表現では、量子状態はベクトルであり、量子Gate（ゲート）（次のセクションで説明）はベクトルを変換する行列となります。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For a single qubit, the vector form of the states are chosen to be:\n"
"$$\\vert 0\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{pmatrix}$$\n"
"$$\\vert 1\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{pmatrix}$$\n"
"In this way, an arbitrary state $\\vert \\psi\\rangle = a\\vert 0\\rangle+b\\vert 1\\rangle$ can be written as\n"
"$$\\vert \\psi\\rangle =\\begin{pmatrix}a \\\\ b\\end{pmatrix}$$\n"
msgstr ""
"1つのQubitについて、各状態のベクトル形式は次のように選ばれます：\n"
"$$\\vert 0\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{pmatrix}$$\n"
"$$\\vert 1\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{pmatrix}$$\n"
"このようにして、任意の状態$\\vert \\psi\\rangle = a\\vert 0\\rangle+b\\vert 1\\rangle$は次のように書けます：\n"
"$$\\vert \\psi\\rangle =\\begin{pmatrix}a \\\\ b\\end{pmatrix}$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a general, $n$-qubit state, we will need a $2^n$-dimensional vector, with basis states ordered as you might expect, in ascending binary value:\n"
msgstr "一般的な$n$Qubit状態では、$2^n$次元のベクトルが必要であり、基底状態は二進数の値の昇順に並べられます：\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert 0 \\dots 000\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\vdots \\\\ 0\\end{pmatrix}, \\vert 0 \\dots 001 \\rangle = \\vert 1 \\dots 110\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}0 \\\\ \\vdots \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{pmatrix}, \\vert 1 \\dots 111 \\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}0 \\\\ \\vdots \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\\\ 1\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert 0 \\dots 000\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\vdots \\\\ 0\\end{pmatrix}, \\vert 0 \\dots 001 \\rangle = \\vert 1 \\dots 110\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}0 \\\\ \\vdots \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{pmatrix}, \\vert 1 \\dots 111 \\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}0 \\\\ \\vdots \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\\\ 1\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With this choice of vector notation in mind, we can introduce our needed quantum gates, their effects on quantum states, and their matrix forms.\n"
msgstr "このベクトル記法を念頭に置いて、必要な量子Gate（ゲート）、量子状態への作用、および行列形式を紹介します。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-4}"
msgstr "理解度チェック {#check-your-understanding-4}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There are four computational basis states for a two-qubit system. Write out each one in both ket and vector notations.\n"
msgstr "2Qubit系には4つの計算基底状態があります。それぞれをケット記法とベクトル記法の両方で書き出してください。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: dropped, JSX/HTML tags differ from English: $$ \vert
# 00\rangle = \begin{pmatrix}1 \\ 0 \\ 0 \\ 0\end{pma
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert 00\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{pmatrix}, \\vert 01 \\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{pmatrix}, \\dots, \\vert 10\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{pmatrix}, \\vert 11 \\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\\\ 1\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Gates $\\rightarrow$ quantum gates {#gates-rightarrow-quantum-gates}"
msgstr "Gate（ゲート） $\\rightarrow$ 量子Gate（ゲート） {#gates-rightarrow-quantum-gates}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Just as classical gates such as NOT, AND, OR, and XOR can be combined to build arbitrary classical circuits, quantum gates play the same role in quantum computing. Because qubits have additional quantum mechanical features, quantum gates are correspondingly richer. While we can still describe their action on the basis states $|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$ with a truth table, this does not capture the whole picture. For quantum gates, it is often more natural to use a matrix representation, since they also act on superpositions of basis states.\n"
msgstr "NOT、AND、OR、XORなどの古典的なGate（ゲート）を組み合わせて任意の古典Circuit（回路）を構築できるように、量子Gate（ゲート）は量子コンピューティングにおいて同じ役割を果たします。Qubitには量子力学的な追加的特徴があるため、量子Gate（ゲート）はそれに対応してより豊富です。基底状態$|0\\rangle$と$|1\\rangle$への作用は真理値表で記述できますが、それでは全体像を捉えきれません。量子Gate（ゲート）では、基底状態の重ね合わせにも作用するため、行列表現を使用する方が自然なことが多いです。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Below we will introduce the most common quantum gates and how they transform the qubits they interact with. When applicable, we’ll connect them back to familiar classical gates.\n"
msgstr "以下では、最も一般的な量子Gate（ゲート）と、それらが相互作用するQubitをどのように変換するかを紹介します。該当する場合は、馴染みのある古典的なGate（ゲート）と結び付けて説明します。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Single-qubit gates {#single-qubit-gates}"
msgstr "1量子ビットゲート {#single-qubit-gates}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**$X$ gate**: This is the quantum equivalent of a NOT operation. Its truth table looks exactly like the classical NOT gate:\n"
msgstr "**$X$ ゲート**: 量子版のNOT演算です。真理値表は古典的なNOTゲートとまったく同じです。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Input | Output |\n"
"| :------- | -------: |\n"
"| $\\vert 0\\rangle$      | $\\vert 1\\rangle$  |\n"
"| $\\vert 1\\rangle$  | $\\vert 0\\rangle$  |\n"
msgstr ""
"| 入力 | 出力 |\n"
"| :------- | -------: |\n"
"| $\\vert 0\\rangle$      | $\\vert 1\\rangle$  |\n"
"| $\\vert 1\\rangle$  | $\\vert 0\\rangle$  |\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "And the matrix representation:\n"
msgstr "行列表現は次のとおりです。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$X=\\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\end{pmatrix}$$\n"
msgstr "$$X=\\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\end{pmatrix}$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In Qiskit, creating a circuit with an $X$ gate looks like this:\n"
msgstr "Qiskitで $X$ ゲートを含むCircuitを作成するには次のようにします。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/modules/quantum-mechanics/get-started-with-qiskit/extracted-outputs/6c215e46-26cb-4e10-a1d7-2eecd2c18294-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![前のコードセルの出力](/learning/images/modules/quantum-mechanics/get-started-with-qiskit/extracted-outputs/6c215e46-26cb-4e10-a1d7-2eecd2c18294-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this very simple circuit diagram, the qubit is represented by a wire, the black horizontal line, and the gate shows up as a box on that wire.\n"
msgstr "この非常にシンプルなCircuit図では、Qubitはワイヤー（黒い水平線）で表されており、ゲートはそのワイヤー上のボックスとして表示されます。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "__Hadamard gate:__ Creates a superposition state. Truth table:\n"
msgstr "__Hadamardゲート:__ 重ね合わせ状態を生成します。真理値表:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Input | Output |\n"
"| :------- | -------: |\n"
"| $\\vert 0\\rangle$      | $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left(\\vert 0\\rangle+\\vert 1\\rangle\\right)$  |\n"
"| $\\vert 1\\rangle$  | $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left(\\vert 0\\rangle-\\vert 1\\rangle\\right)$  |\n"
msgstr ""
"| 入力 | 出力 |\n"
"| :------- | -------: |\n"
"| $\\vert 0\\rangle$      | $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left(\\vert 0\\rangle+\\vert 1\\rangle\\right)$  |\n"
"| $\\vert 1\\rangle$  | $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left(\\vert 0\\rangle-\\vert 1\\rangle\\right)$  |\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Matrix representation:\n"
"$$H=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\end{pmatrix}$$\n"
msgstr ""
"行列表現:\n"
"$$H=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\end{pmatrix}$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A circuit with a Hadamard gate is made as follows:\n"
msgstr "HadamardゲートをもつCircuitは次のように作成します。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/modules/quantum-mechanics/get-started-with-qiskit/extracted-outputs/1a009015-4ced-47e4-a18d-d0685e4cab47-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![前のコードセルの出力](/learning/images/modules/quantum-mechanics/get-started-with-qiskit/extracted-outputs/1a009015-4ced-47e4-a18d-d0685e4cab47-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**$Z$ gate**: Adds a phase shift of $\\Delta \\phi = \\pi$  to the $|1\\rangle$ state:\n"
msgstr "**$Z$ ゲート**: $|1\\rangle$ 状態に $\\Delta \\phi = \\pi$ の位相シフトを加えます。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Input | Output |\n"
"| :------- | -------: |\n"
"| $\\vert 0\\rangle$      | $\\vert 0\\rangle$  |\n"
"| $\\vert 1\\rangle$  | $-\\vert 1\\rangle$  |\n"
